          "prompt": "vier",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["ee as in see", "eye as in pie", "ear as in hear"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-e8",
          "type": "LISTEN_TYPE",
          "text": "drei",
          "translation": "three"
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-e9",
          "type": "LISTEN_TYPE",
          "text": "neu",
          "translation": "new"
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-e10",
          "type": "SHADOW",
          "text": "Mein Haus ist neu.",
          "translation": "My house is new.",
          "hint": "ei = eye, au = ow, eu = oy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3-consonants",
      "title": "Tricky consonants",
      "kind": "SOUNDS",
      "introduces": [],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "s3-e1",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "W, V, Z and S",
          "body": "- **w** sounds like English *v*: *Wasser, wie*\n- **v** usually sounds like English *f*: *Vater, viel*\n- **z** sounds like the *ts* in *cats*: *Zeit, zehn*\n- **s** before a vowel sounds like English *z*: *Sonne, sieben*",
          "mouthShapes": [
            { "shape": "TEETH_ON_LIP", "label": "w and v", "caption": "Upper teeth rest on the lower lip" }
          ],
          "examples": [
            { "text": "Wasser", "translation": "water", "hint": "VAS-ser" },
            { "text": "Vater", "translation": "father", "hint": "FAH-ter" },
            { "text": "Zeit", "translation": "time", "hint": "tsite" },
            { "text": "sieben", "translation": "seven", "hint": "ZEE-ben" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e2",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "instruction": "The W in this word sounds like English…",
          "prompt": "Wasser",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["v", "w", "f"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e3",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "instruction": "The Z in this word sounds like…",
          "prompt": "zehn",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["ts as in cats", "z as in zoo", "s as in sun"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e4",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "The two ch sounds",
          "body": "German *ch* has two sounds — and neither is the *ch* in *church*.\n\n- After **a, o, u, au** it's a rough sound at the back of the throat, like Scottish *loch*: *Buch, auch*\n- Everywhere else it's a soft hiss, like the *h* in *huge* said with force: *ich, nicht, Milch*",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "auch", "translation": "also", "hint": "back of the throat" },
            { "text": "Buch", "translation": "book", "hint": "back of the throat" },
            { "text": "ich", "translation": "I", "hint": "soft hiss" },
            { "text": "nicht", "translation": "not", "hint": "soft hiss" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e5",
          "type": "LISTEN_CHOOSE",
          "options": ["ich", "ach"],
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e6",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "sp, st, r and word endings",
          "body": "- At the **start** of a word, **sp** and **st** sound like *shp* and *sht*: *sprechen, Straße*\n- The German **r** at the start of a syllable is made at the back of the throat, close to a soft gargle: *rot*\n- At the end of a word, **-er** sounds like the *a* in *sofa*: *Vater, Mutter*\n- **b, d, g** at the end of a word sound like **p, t, k**: *Tag* sounds like *tahk*, *Hund* like *hoont*",
          "examples": [
            { "text": "sprechen", "translation": "to speak", "hint": "SHPRE-chen" },
            { "text": "Straße", "translation": "street", "hint": "SHTRAH-se" },
            { "text": "rot", "translation": "red" },
            { "text": "Tag", "translation": "day", "hint": "ends in a k sound" },
            { "text": "Hund", "translation": "dog", "hint": "ends in a t sound" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e7",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "instruction": "How does this word start?",
          "prompt": "Straße",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["sht", "st", "s"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e8",
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "instruction": "How does the final g sound?",
          "prompt": "Tag",
          "promptLanguage": "TARGET",
          "options": ["like k", "like the g in go", "silent"],
          "optionsLanguage": "BASE",
          "answerIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e9",
          "type": "LISTEN_TYPE",
          "text": "Wasser",
          "translation": "water"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e10",
          "type": "SHADOW",
          "text": "Ich spreche ein bisschen Deutsch.",
          "translation": "I speak a little German.",
          "hint": "ich = soft hiss, sp = shp, eu = oy."
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-e11",
          "type": "SHADOW",
          "text": "Wie viel Uhr ist es?",
          "translation": "What time is it?",
          "hint": "w = v and v = f: vee feel oor.",
          "mouthShapes": [
            { "shape": "TEETH_ON_LIP", "label": "w, v", "caption": "Teeth on lower lip for both" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
